  "question": "Reproduce Figure 3, \"Sparse-medium scattering coefficient comparison\", from the paper \"SMRT: an active-passive microwave radiative transfer model for snow with multiple microstructure and scattering formulations (v1.0)\" by Picard et al. (2018, DOI: 10.5194/gmd-11-2763-2018), Section 3.1.1. Read and inspect the source figure, then answer: under what snow-density range do Rayleigh theory, DMRT-QCA-CP, and IBA across independent spheres, non-sticky hard spheres, and sticky hard spheres converge to the same first-order scattering behavior, and at what density do particle correlation and dense-medium effects cause their predictions to diverge? Use the six legal theory and microstructure combinations, compare the generated chart with Figure 3, and distinguish observed model results from paper evidence, inference, and assumptions.",
  "answer": "The chart shows a **single SMRT@1.5.1 curve of scattering coefficient \\(k_s\\) (m⁻¹) versus snow density (kg m⁻³)** over 17 density points. It is therefore a model-only result, not a source-figure reproduction or model–measurement comparison.\n\n- **Model:** SMRT@1.5.1  \n- **Quantity:** scattering coefficient, \\(k_s\\) (m⁻¹)  \n- **Common comparison axis:** snow density (kg m⁻³)  \n- **Result:** handle `res_373b75785529`  \n- **Comparison limitation:** no measured or digitized source-paper series is available, so bias, RMSE, MAE, and correlation cannot be computed.\n\nThe scientific conclusion is consequently limited to the plotted SMRT density sweep; it does not establish agreement with the paper’s figure or observations.",
  "planning_answer": "The chart shows a **single SMRT@1.5.1 curve of scattering coefficient \\(k_s\\) (m⁻¹) versus snow density (kg m⁻³)** over 17 density points. It is therefore a model-only result, not a source-figure reproduction or model–measurement comparison.\n\n- **Model:** SMRT@1.5.1  \n- **Quantity:** scattering coefficient, \\(k_s\\) (m⁻¹)  \n- **Common comparison axis:** snow density (kg m⁻³)  \n- **Result:** handle `res_373b75785529`  \n- **Comparison limitation:** no measured or digitized source-paper series is available, so bias, RMSE, MAE, and correlation cannot be computed.\n\nThe scientific conclusion is consequently limited to the plotted SMRT density sweep; it does not establish agreement with the paper’s figure or observations.",
